# `ledger-entry-type` Standalone Wire Specification

The codec maps a canonical ledger-entry format name such as `AccountRoot` to
its protocol `LedgerEntryType` and writes that value as exactly two big-endian
bytes. Decode performs the reverse lookup and rejects unregistered values.

The input is a name, not a decimal type code. The registered values originate
in `ledger_entries.macro`; deprecated/internal enum values that are not loaded
into `LedgerFormats` are not silently accepted. There is no field header in
the standalone payload.

